    "caption": "BlackBerry once dominated the smartphone market.\n\nIts physical keyboard became a symbol of business communication.\n\nThen smartphones changed.\n\nTouchscreens, apps, and new ecosystems transformed what consumers expected. BlackBerry struggled to keep pace and eventually moved away from making its own phones.\n\nBut the company didn't disappear. It transformed its business.\n\nThe lesson?\n\nYour biggest competitive advantage today can become your biggest weakness tomorrow if you stop adapting.\n\nAre businesses better off protecting what made them successful or constantly reinventing themselves?\n\n#BlackBerry #Technology #BusinessStrategy #Innovation #BusinessCaseStudy #Entrepreneurship #Simpledeav"
